#!perl
our $VERSION = '0.01';
use Game::Senet::Terminal;
exit Game::Senet::Terminal->run(@ARGV);

__END__

=head1 NAME

senet - Senet, the race game of ancient Egypt, in a terminal

=head1 SYNOPSIS

    senet
    senet --rules skyruk --level 2
    senet --mode hotseat --pieces 7
    senet --ascii --no-pick
    senet --help

=head1 DESCRIPTION

Thirty houses in three rows of ten, the track a reversed S, five pieces a side
and four throwing sticks. You play light against the program unless told
otherwise. See L<Game::Senet::Terminal> for every option and the keys.

=head1 EXIT STATUS

0 when the game was won, drawn or left; 1 when you lost to the program; 2 for
an option or a value it does not know.

